# AI Agent Guardrails for exenova.dk-astro

1. **NO JS FRAMEWORKS:** Do not install or use React, Vue, Svelte, or Alpine.js. Use pure HTML5 and Astro components ONLY.
2. **TAILWIND CSS:** This project uses Tailwind CSS for styling. Use utility classes strictly. Custom CSS in `<style>` tags should be avoided unless absolutely necessary.
3. **MANDATORY JSDOC:** Every component's `Props` interface and frontmatter MUST have a JSDoc block explaining its purpose.
4. **NPM ONLY:** Use `npm` for all package management.
5. **PLUGIN POLICY:** Use battle-hardened, official plugins for Tailwind (e.g., @tailwindcss/typography) and Astro (e.g., sitemap, mdx) to avoid reinventing the wheel. HOWEVER, these must be strictly **build-time** or have a negligible frontend JavaScript footprint. Heavy client-side UI libraries (like Headless UI or Alpine) remain strictly forbidden.
6. **GLOBAL DATA:** Do not hardcode the author's name, email, social links, or default SEO strings. Always import and use `SITE_CONFIG` from `src/config/site.ts`. (Note: High-level toggles like showMenubar and createSitemap are managed centrally in the "config" block of package.json).
7. **SEPARATION OF CONCERNS:** Keep `.astro` files focused on UI. Abstract data fetching/sorting to `src/utils/content.ts` and heavy client-side logic to `src/scripts/`.
8. **ICONOGRAPHY:** All SVG icons live in `src/assets/icons/` and are imported via `?raw`. The `src/components/Icon.astro` component handles fetching, sanitization (stripping width/height/fill/stroke, injecting `currentColor`), and rendering directly. Never hardcode SVG markup directly in components.
9. **TAILWIND V4:** Do not create `tailwind.config.js/mjs`. All theme configuration belongs in `src/styles/global.css`.
10. **NO HTML IN JS:** Never write HTML markup inside TypeScript/JavaScript strings. Use HTML `<template>` tags for client-side rendering.
11. **PAGE STRUCTURE & 75-LINE RULE:** Pages and Blocks are strictly orchestrators. If ANY Astro component's HTML template exceeds 75 lines, you MUST extract logical sections into sub-components. Complex HTML must be hidden behind clean, strictly-typed Props interfaces.
12. **BUILD-TIME LOGIC:** Calculate dynamic UI elements (like breadcrumbs or active states) in Astro frontmatter. Do not use client-side JS for static UI generation.
13. **TYPOGRAPHY:** Never use `font-sans`, `font-serif`, or `text-*` size utility classes directly in templates for standard text. All UI text must use the `type-*` utility classes defined in `global.css` (e.g., `<h1 class="type-h1 text-theme-text">`). Markdown text is handled automatically by `.prose`.
14. **STYLE GUIDE ENFORCEMENT:** Whenever a new UI component or visual element is created or modified, you MUST add or update its showcase in `src/components/StyleGuideViewer.astro`.
15. **COMPONENT TAXONOMY:** Enforce Atomic Design. Isolate base primitives (Buttons, Typography, Tags) from composite blocks (Hero, Cards, Headers, PageTitle). Every component MUST have a TypeScript `Props` interface defined, even if empty or just accepting `class?: string`.
16. **ENCAPSULATION & COMPLEXITY:** Hide complexity inside components. Pages are strict orchestrators (Smart Components, Dumb Pages). UI components must handle their own data formatting internally (e.g., a component expecting a date should accept a raw ISO string and format it internally, not expect a pre-formatted string).
17. **ZERO-MARGIN COMPONENTS & STRUCTURAL RHYTHM:** All UI elements, including text elements, MUST NOT apply exterior margins (e.g., `mt-*`, `mb-*`, `my-*`) to their outermost elements. Components must be completely ignorant of their surroundings. All spacing between sibling elements MUST be dictated by the parent container using the centralized CSS utilities (`rhythm-section`, `rhythm-stack`, `rhythm-group`). Do not use ad-hoc layout spacing.
18. **THEME & COLOR CASCADE:** Components MUST NOT accept `inverted`, `theme`, `textColor`, or any color-related props for visual styling. Use semantic theme tokens (`text-theme-text`, `bg-theme-bg`, `text-theme-muted`, `border-theme-border`) exclusively. Color is resolved via CSS cascade from the `data-theme` attribute on `<body>`, set by `BaseLayout`. To show a component in a different color context, wrap it in a `<div data-theme="...">` container rather than adding props to the component itself.